ID}&topic=${e://Field/Topic}&condition=${e://Field/Condition}&partner=${e://Field/PartnerGender}&party=${e://Field/Party}&ideology=${e://Field/PartnerIdeology}&rid=${e://Field/ResponseID}&owntopic=${e://Field/TopicOwn}","EmailThankYou":"false","ThankYouEmailMessageLibrary":null,"ThankYouEmailMessage":null,"ValidateMessage":"false","ValidationMessageLibrary":null,"InactiveSurvey":"DefaultMessage","PartialDeletion":"+1 day","PartialDataCloseAfter":"LastActivity","InactiveMessageLibrary":null,"InactiveMessage":null,"AvailableLanguages":{"EN":[]},"ProtectSelectionIds":true,"SurveyName":"ConvoLab presurvey"}},{"SurveyID":"SV_cTT6h3GdIPz4LUG","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID1","SecondaryAttribute":"RESEARCH PARTICIPANT CONSENT STUDY2025-00000385 Using AI to Train Political Dialogue Principal In...","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"<b>RESEARCH PARTICIPANT CONSENT\nSTUDY2025-00000385</b><br>Using AI to Train Political Dialogue\n<br>Principal Investigator: Dr. Daniel Schiff\n<br>Co-Principal Investigator: Hanna Sistek\n<br>Department: Political Science\n<br>Institution: Purdue University&nbsp;<br><br>You are being asked to participate in a research study. The purpose of this research is to explore questions around dialogue, education and artificial intelligence (AI). We use this general description, since some research requires that the full purpose of the study not be explained before you participate. We will give you a full explanation at the end of the study in a debriefing form. The total amount of time you will be in this study is approximately 15 minutes. During your participation, you will be asked to complete a brief survey about your political views and attitudes toward AI, have a conversation about a political topic with an AI partner, and answer follow-up questions about your experience. Taking part in this research involves possible emotional discomfort from discussing political topics and a minor risk of breach of confidentiality, that are no greater than typically encountered in daily life. There may be direct benefits to you and society. \n<br><br>Please read this form carefully and ask the researchers to explain anything you do not understand before you agree to be in the study.\n<br><br><b>Key Information\n</b><br><b>What is the study about?</b> \nYou are being asked to participate in a research study about how artificial intelligence (AI) can be used in practicing political dialogue. We are testing an AI dialogue tool which lets you have a conversation about politics with an AI partner. \nYou are eligible because you are an adult (18 years or older) recruited through the Prolific research platform.\n<br><br><b>What will I do if I choose to be in this study?</b>\nYou will be asked to first answer a short set of questions about your political views, interest in current affairs, and attitudes toward AI. You will then have a conversation about a political topic of your choice with an AI partner that has different views from you. After the dialogue, you will answer some follow-up questions about your experience, views and basic demographic information.\nAll data will be collected through Qualtrics (online survey) and the AI app.\nPlease do not provide any sensitive identifiable information that would allow your identity to readily be ascertained, directly or through identifiers provided in your responses.\n<br><br><b>How long will I be in the study?</b>\nYour participation will involve a single session lasting approximately 15 minutes. There is no follow-up.\n\nPlease consider the risks of taking part in this study before you decide to participate.\nBreach of confidentiality is always a risk with data, but we will take precautions to minimize this risk as described below.\n<br><br><table style=\"width:100%; border-collapse: collapse; border: 1px solid #000;\">\n<tbody><tr>\n<th style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px; text-align: left; background-color: #f2f2f2;\"><strong>Possible risk(s)</strong></th>\n<th style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px; text-align: left; background-color: #f2f2f2;\"><strong>How we\u2019re minimizing these risks</strong></th>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px;\">You may feel uncomfortable discussing political topics or having your views challenged by the AI partner.</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px;\">You choose the topic for discussion. You may skip survey questions you do not want to answer. You may stop the dialogue or withdraw from the study at any time.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px;\">Your political opinions or dialogue content could be disclosed if data security were breached.</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px;\">No names or direct identifiers are collected. Data is stored in secure, password-protected cloud storage (e.g., Purdue Box, Dropbox, or similar). IP addresses are anonymized. Only the research team members listed on the IRB protocol have access to the data.</td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px;\">You may feel uneasy about sharing sensitive political opinions, even in a research context.</td>\n<td style=\"border: 1px solid #000; padding: 8px;\">The research team cannot link your responses to your identity. You are instructed not to share personally identifiable information during the dialogue.</td></tr></tbody></table><br><b>Are there any benefits?</b>\nWe cannot promise any direct benefits for taking part in this study. However, you may find the experience of practicing dialogue with an AI partner interesting or personally valuable. \n\n<br><br><b>How will the researchers protect my information?</b>\nWe will not collect your name, email address, or any direct identifiers. The platform mediates your identity; the research team only receives pseudonymous Prolific IDs, which are treated as potentially identifiable and will be immediately replaced with our own random participant IDs upon data download. IP addresses are anonymized in Qualtrics settings. Data will be stored in secure, password-protected cloud storage (e.g., Purdue Box). Only the Principal Investigator, Daniel Schiff, Co-PI, Hanna Sistek and other members of the research team will have access to the data.  \n\n<br><br><b>Who will see the information collected in this research?</b>\nEfforts will be made to limit the use and disclosure of your personal information, including research study records, to people who have a need to review this information. We cannot promise complete secrecy. There are reasons why information about you may be used or seen by other people beyond the research team during or after this study. Examples include:\n\u2022  Purdue University departments responsible for regulatory and research oversight, and the US DHHS Office for Human Research Protections.\nOnly the research team will have access to research records collected for this research. Before the data is shared outside the research team, any potentially identifying information will be removed. Once identifying data has been removed, the data may be used by the research team, or shared with other researchers, for both related and unrelated research purposes in the future. Your anonymized data may also be made available in online data repositories such as the Open Science Framework, which allow other researchers and interested parties to use the data for further analysis.\n\n<br><br><b>Will I receive payment or other incentive?</b>\nAfter completing the survey, you will be provided with the compensation agreed upon between you and the market research panel for which you are a member. \n\n<br><br><b>Are there costs to me for participation?</b>\nThere are no anticipated costs to participate in this research.\n\n<br><br><b>What are my rights as a research participant in this study?</b>\nResearch studies include only people who choose to take part. You can tell us that you don\u2019t want to be in this study. You can start the study and then choose to stop the study later. This will not affect your relationship with the investigator. You may skip any questions you do not wish to answer.\n\n<br><br><b>How might the information collected in this study be shared in the future?</b>\nWe will keep the information we collect about you during this research study for study recordkeeping and for potential use in future research projects. De-identified data from this study may be shared with the research community, with journals in which study results are published, and with databases and data repositories used for research. We will remove or code any personal information that could directly identify you before the study data are shared. Despite these measures, we cannot guarantee the anonymity of your personal data.\nThe results of this study could be shared in articles and presentations but will not include any information that identifies you.\n\n<br><br><b>Who can I contact if I have questions about the study?</b>\nIf you have questions, comments, or concerns about this research project, you can talk to the Principal Investigator, Dr. Daniel Schiff: dschiff@purdue.edu or Co-PI, Dr. Hanna Sistek hsistek@purdue.edu, 765-464-9062.\nTo report anonymously via Purdue\u2019s Hotline, see www.purdue.edu/hotline\nIf you have questions about your rights while taking part in the study or have concerns about the treatment of research participants, please call the Human Research Protection Program at (765) 494-5942, email irb@purdue.edu, or write to:\n\nHuman Research Protection Program\nPurdue University\nSeng Liang Wang Hall\n516 Northwestern Ave\nWest Lafayette, IN 47906\n\n<br><br><b>Documentation of Informed Consent</b>\nI have had the opportunity to read this consent form and have the research study explained.  I have had the opportunity to ask questions about the research study, and my questions have been answered.  I am prepared to participate in the research study described above.  I will be offered a copy of this consent form.","DataExportTag":"consent","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"RESEARCH PARTICIPANT CONSENT STUDY2025-00000385 Using AI to Train Political Dialogue Principal In...","Choices":{"4":{"Display":"I am 18 years of age or older, and I consent to participate in this study."},"5":{"Display":"I am under 18 years of age, or I do not consent to participate in this study."}},"ChoiceOrder":["4","5"],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":6,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID1","DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"AnalyzeChoices":{"5":"No"}}},{"SurveyID":"SV_cTT6h3GdIPz4LUG","Element":"SQ","PrimaryAttribute":"QID10","SecondaryAttribute":"Would you call yourself a strong Republican or not a very strong Republican?","TertiaryAttribute":null,"Payload":{"QuestionText":"Would you call yourself a strong Republican or not a very strong Republican?","DataExportTag":"stwrep","QuestionType":"MC","Selector":"SAVR","SubSelector":"TX","Configuration":{"QuestionDescriptionOption":"UseText"},"QuestionDescription":"Would you call yourself a strong Republican or not a very strong Republican?","Choices":{"1":{"Display":"Strong Republican"},"2":{"Display":"Not very strong Republican"}},"ChoiceOrder":[1,2],"Validation":{"Settings":{"ForceResponse":"ON","ForceResponseType":"ON","Type":"None"}},"Language":[],"NextChoiceId":3,"NextAnswerId":1,"QuestionID":"QID10","ChoiceGroups":{"cg_1":{"ChoiceGroupOrder":[1],"GroupLabel":"Strong Republican","Options":{"HideTitle":true,"Selection":"SAWithinQuestion"}},"cg_2":{"ChoiceGroupOrder":[2],"GroupLabel":"Not very strong Republican","Options":{"HideTitle":true,"Selection":"SAWithinQuestion"}}},"ChoiceGroupOrder":["cg_1","cg_2"],"DataVisibility":{"Private":false,"Hidden":false},"DisplayLogic":{"0":{"0":{"ChoiceLocator